{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>He made him ride on the heights of the earth.</b> The land of Canaan, which is at the center of the inhabited world, and 'he made him ride' is a figure of speech." "<b>Bamotei.</b> The vav does not change from the paradigm of על במותימו תדרוך, and there is none like it, and 'the rich' — במותיו." "<b>Tenuvot.</b> Like 'fruit,' from the root חיל כי ינוב." "<b>Shaddai.</b> An epithet of the Name on the pattern of חכם, and the yod is in place of the heh, like the vav of הייתי, and the proof is יעלוז שדי, which is singular." "<b>He suckled him with honey from the rock.</b> By way of parable, like 'the mountains shall be wrapped in fatness,' and the meaning is the abundance of honey and oil. For they were brought from the land of Canaan, for so it is written." "<b>Flint of rock.</b> The lamed is rafeh, for it is attached, and it is the opposite of צור החלמיש, and likewise חרבות צורים with צור חרבו."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra cites the paradigm form from Deuteronomy 33:29; the manuscript variant reading 'רשעים' (wicked) is noted against 'עשיר' (rich). The word in Psalms is וּבַמּוֹתָיו (Psalms 18:34).", 5 "The phrase 'והנה הוא הפך' is rendered hyper-literally; the argument is compressed and turns on the forms with/without the article on חלמיש."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:58.452811861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}